{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":502,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"A man who isolates himself pursues selfishness, and defies all sound judgment.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1568},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":503,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"A fool has no delight in understanding, but only in revealing his own opinion.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1571},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":504,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"When wickedness comes, contempt also comes, and with shame comes disgrace.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1574},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":505,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"The words of a man’s mouth are like deep waters. The fountain of wisdom is like a flowing brook.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1577},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":506,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"To be partial to the faces of the wicked is not good, nor to deprive the innocent of justice.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1580},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":507,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"A fool’s lips come into strife, and his mouth invites beatings.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1583},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":508,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are a snare to his soul.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1586},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":509,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"The words of a gossip are like dainty morsels: they go down into a person’s innermost parts.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1589},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":510,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"One who is slack in his work is brother to him who is a master of destruction.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1592},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":511,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"The LORD’s name is a strong tower: the righteous run to him, and are safe.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1595},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":512,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, like an unscalable wall in his own imagination.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1598},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":513,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Before destruction the heart of man is proud, but before honor is humility.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1601},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":514,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"He who answers before he hears, that is folly and shame to him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1604},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":515,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"A man’s spirit will sustain him in sickness, but a crushed spirit, who can bear?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1607},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":516,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"The heart of the discerning gets knowledge. The ear of the wise seeks knowledge.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1610},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":517,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"A man’s gift makes room for him, and brings him before great men.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1613},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":518,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"He who pleads his cause first seems right— until another comes and questions him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1616},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":519,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"The lot settles disputes, and keeps strong ones apart.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1619},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":520,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"A brother offended is more difficult than a fortified city. Disputes are like the bars of a fortress.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1622},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":521,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"A man’s stomach is filled with the fruit of his mouth. With the harvest of his lips he is satisfied.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1625},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":522,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"Death and life are in the power of the tongue; those who love it will eat its fruit.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1628},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":523,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"Whoever finds a wife finds a good thing, and obtains favor of the LORD.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1631},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":524,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"The poor plead for mercy, but the rich answer harshly.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1634},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":525,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"A man of many companions may be ruined, but there is a friend who sticks closer than a brother.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1637}]}